From 31157d25caf7284080cdb5d86ab7e8e438120fd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gobbajogger <255244738+gobbajogger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:52:34 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: express strict cycle costs as 360 MHz sixteenths

The cost table was in eighths of a 240 MHz cycle, so --mhz 360 finished
work 1.5x sooner than the SMK-37. Odd eighths are not integers times 1.5,
so costs are now sixteenths of a 360 MHz cycle (cost16 = cost8 * 3),
XIP misses are 300*24 ticks, and FM1_STRICT uses 16 ticks per cycle.
TIMER4 stays 24 MHz of emulated time. Default clock is 360, including
the plugin (v0.2.0 240/320/400 indices are unchanged).
